From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackParrot Context Resume Experiment <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sched: trigger BlackParrot shared instruction replay

Start the machine-configured, address-free shared instruction prefix at the
earliest common scheduler entry. The custom supervisor CSR is specific to the
experimental BlackParrot platform; other architectures compile no instruction.
---
 kernel/sched/core.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
index 802551e00000..802551e00001 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -6576,6 +6576,13 @@ static void __sched notrace __schedule(unsigned int sched_mode)
 	struct rq *rq;
 	int cpu;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_RISCV
+	/* Physical prefix contents are machine-owned. Supervisor software can
+	 * only launch the configured table and therefore supplies no address.
+	 */
+	asm volatile("csrw 0x5c0, zero" ::: "memory");
+#endif
+
 	cpu = smp_processor_id();
 	rq = cpu_rq(cpu);
 	prev = rq->curr;
-- 
